Yo C gurus and dev.teamsters:

Today, trying to start up a saved game produced the message "Saved
level is out date" whereupon my saved file went to the bitbucket and a
new game was begun. (That was a good game that got clobbered too:
Fadila-V had Mjollnir, blessed bag of holding, blessed cloak of
displacement, grey dragon scale mail *and* lots of intrinsic AC from
the minetown priest, and had had several run-ins with wraiths who
kindly left corpses behind, and as for uncursed potions of gain level,
the place was absolutely littered with them.)

So why did this happen? The relevant piece of code from unixunix.c (and
BTW this is 3.1.0 and the machine is an SGI runnig Irix 4.0.5):

int
uptodate(fd)
int fd;
{
        if(fstat(fd, &buf)) {
                pline("Cannot get status of saved level? ");
                wait_synch();
                return(0);
        }
        if(buf.st_mtime < hbuf.st_mtime) {
                pline("Saved level is out of date. ");
                wait_synch();
                return(0);
        }
        return(1);
}
